Fix the following CTL2 Denormalizer transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

The Denormalizer groups its input by customer_id (the input is sorted by customer_id) and emits one output record per customer.

Specification:
1. customer_id: the customer of the group.
2. shipped_count: the number of the customer's orders whose status is "SHIPPED". Status values are always uppercase.
3. shipped_total: the sum of order_amount over those shipped orders. A null order_amount counts as 0, and the order is still counted in shipped_count.
4. avg_shipped: shipped_total / shipped_count, rounded half-up to 2 decimal places. A customer can have no shipped orders at all. Then shipped_count is 0, shipped_total is 0 and avg_shipped is null.
5. last_order_date: the latest order_date among all of this customer's orders, whatever their status. order_date is never null and is always later than 2000-01-01.
6. statuses: the distinct status values of this customer's orders, in the order they were first seen, joined with "," (e.g. "NEW,SHIPPED").

Port 0 (in):
<Metadata id="M0"><Record name="CustomerOrder" type="delimited"><Field name="customer_id" type="long" nullable="false"/><Field name="order_id" type="long" nullable="false"/><Field name="order_date" type="date" nullable="false"/><Field name="status" type="string" nullable="false"/><Field name="order_amount" type="decimal" length="12" scale="2" nullable="true"/></Record></Metadata>

Port 0 (out):
<Metadata id="M1"><Record name="CustomerSummary" type="delimited"><Field name="customer_id" type="long" nullable="false"/><Field name="shipped_count" type="integer" nullable="false"/><Field name="shipped_total" type="decimal" length="12" scale="2" nullable="false"/><Field name="avg_shipped" type="decimal" length="12" scale="2" nullable="true"/><Field name="last_order_date" type="date" nullable="false"/><Field name="statuses" type="string" nullable="false"/></Record></Metadata>

```ctl
//#CTL2
long customerId;
integer shippedCount;
decimal shippedTotal;
date lastOrderDate;
string[] statuses;

function integer append() {
    customerId = $in.0.customer_id;
    if ($in.0.status == "SHIPPED") {
        shippedCount++;
        shippedTotal = shippedTotal + $in.0.order_amount;
    }
    if ($in.0.order_date > lastOrderDate) {
        lastOrderDate = $in.0.order_date;
    }
    if (!statuses.contains($in.0.status)) {
        push(statuses, $in.0.status);
    }
    return OK;
}

function integer transform() {
    $out.0.customer_id = customerId;
    $out.0.shipped_count = shippedCount;
    $out.0.shipped_total = shippedTotal;
    $out.0.avg_shipped = round(shippedTotal / shippedCount, 2);
    $out.0.last_order_date = lastOrderDate;
    $out.0.statuses = join(",", statuses);
    return OK;
}

function void clean() {
    shippedCount = 0;
    shippedTotal = 0D;
    clear(statuses);
}
```

