tests.user_message:
Fix the following CTL2 Partition transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

The Partition routes shipments to five output ports. Records pass through unchanged; the Partition only chooses the port. The rules are checked in this order, and the first one that matches decides:
1. promised_date is null, or ship_date is earlier than the ship_date of the previous input record (the input should arrive sorted by ship_date): port 3 (manual review).
2. Express: service is "EXPRESS" and promised_date is at most 2 calendar days after ship_date: port 0. service may arrive in any letter case and with surrounding spaces ("EXPRESS", "Express ", " express"). The other service values are "STANDARD", "EXPRESS_SAVER" and "NO_EXPRESS", and none of them is express. Example: shipped 2026-03-10, promised 2026-03-12 is express; promised 2026-03-13 is not.
3. Heavy: weight_kg is 30 or more: port 1.
4. Everything else alternates between port 2 and port 4: the first record that reaches this rule goes to port 2, the second to port 4, the third to port 2, and so on. Only records that reach this rule count toward the alternation.
5. A record whose routing fails for any reason goes to port 3.

Input port 0:
<Metadata id="M0"><Record name="Shipment" type="delimited"><Field name="shipment_id" type="long" nullable="false"/><Field name="service" type="string" nullable="false"/><Field name="ship_date" type="date" nullable="false"/><Field name="promised_date" type="date" nullable="true"/><Field name="weight_kg" type="decimal" length="10" scale="3" nullable="false"/><Field name="dest_country" type="string" nullable="false"/></Record></Metadata>

Output ports 0 to 4 carry the same Shipment metadata.

```ctl
//#CTL2
integer turn;
date prevShip;

function integer getOutputPort() {
    turn++;
    boolean outOfOrder = $in.0.ship_date < prevShip;
    prevShip = $in.0.ship_date;
    if ($in.0.promised_date == null || outOfOrder) {
        return 3;
    }
    boolean express = upperCase(trim($in.0.service)) ?= "EXPRESS"
        && dateDiff($in.0.ship_date, $in.0.promised_date, day) <= 2;
    if ($in.0.weight_kg >= 30) {
        return 1;
    }
    if (express) {
        $out.0.route = "EXPRESS";
        return 0;
    }
    return (turn % 2 == 1) ? 2 : 4;
}

function integer getOutputPortOnError(string errorMessage, string stackTrace) {
    return 3;
}
